# arcgis-hub-metric-card
## Overview
The arcgis-hub-metric-card is a wrapper component used to resolve a given metric and then display it through usage of another ArcGIS Web Component. To do this, the arcgis-hub-metric-card utilizes functions to resolve an `IMetric` -- it then renders the `IResolvedMetric` returned by Hub.js.

This component should be used when displaying a metric on a Project or Initiative, or utilizing a layout card that is based around metrics on a Site. This component should also be used when utilizing the arcgis-stat-card to display a metric.

## Examples

### Rendering a static metric in the stat-card
```html
<arcgis-hub-metric-card id="static-metric-card" metric-id="c67890"/>

<script>
    // metric
    const staticMetric = {
      id: "c67890",
      name: "Budget",
      units: "$",
      source: {
        type: 'static-value',
        value: "200,000"
      },
      entityInfo: {
        id: "00c",
        name: "Some project name",
        type: "Hub Project"
      }
    }

    // card config for rendering
    const cardConfig = {
      cardTitle: "This is the title",
      displayType: 'stat-card',
      metricId: "c67890",
      shareable: true,
      shareableByValue: false,
      trailingText: "this is the trailing text...",
      sourceType: "dynamic",
      sourceLink: "link",
      sourceTitle: "title",
      corners: "round",
      valueColor: "#366078"
    }

    // add both to the metric card
    const staticMetricsCard = document.querySelector('#static-metrics-card');
    staticMetricsCard.metric = staticMetric;
    staticMetricsCard.cardConfig = cardConfig;

// add context to the metric card
    document.addEventListener('arcgisAppIdentitySignedIn', (evt) => {
      staticMetricsCard.context = evt.detail;
      showUserInfo(evt.detail.session);
    });

    document.addEventListener('arcgisAppIdentitySignedOut', (evt) => {
      staticMetricsCard.context = evt.detail;
      showUserInfo(evt.detail.session);
    });
</script>
```

### Rendering a service query metric in the stat-card
```html
<arcgis-hub-metric-card id="dynamic-metric-card" metric-id="c67890"/>

<script>
    // metric

    const dynamicMetric = {
      id: "c123456",
      name: "Coastline",
      units: "%",
      source: {
        type: "service-query",
        serviceUrl:
          "https://servicesqa.arcgis.com/T5cZDlfUaBpDnk6P/arcgis/rest/services/2019_US_coastline/FeatureServer",
        layerId: 0,
        field: "FID",
        statistic: "count",
      },
      entityInfo: {
        id: "00c",
        name: "Some Project Name",
        type: "Hub Project",
      },
    };

    // card config for rendering
    const cardConfig = {
      cardTitle: "This is the title",
      displayType: 'stat-card',
      metricId: "c123456",
      shareable: true,
      shareableByValue: false,
      trailingText: "this is the trailing text...",
      sourceType: "dynamic",
      sourceLink: "link",
      sourceTitle: "title",
      corners: "round",
      valueColor: "#366078"
    }

    // add both to the metric card
    const dynamicMetricsCard = document.querySelector('#dynamic-metric-card');
    dynamicMetricsCard.metric = staticMetric;
    dynamicMetricsCard.cardConfig = cardConfig;

// add context to the metric card
    document.addEventListener('arcgisAppIdentitySignedIn', (evt) => {
      dynamicMetricsCard.context = evt.detail;
      showUserInfo(evt.detail.session);
    });

    document.addEventListener('arcgisAppIdentitySignedOut', (evt) => {
      dynamicMetricsCard.context = evt.detail;
      showUserInfo(evt.detail.session);
    });
</script>
```


## Status
The component is currently in development with plans to go into production alongside the new arcgis-stat-card. 
Future functionality will include adding support for an item-query, as well as portal and telemetry queries. 

## Technical
The arcgis-hub-metric-card uses the `resolveMetric` function in Hub.js to resolve the passed in `IMetric metric`. Once this metric is resolved, `IMetricFeature[]` is returned by `resolveMetric`. This list of features will contain right now at most one feature, but when item-query is implemented, it can return multiple features. This/these feature(s) are then displayed utilizing the chosen rendering component, such as the arcgis-stat-card. 

For more information, see [Metric Definition and Resolution documentation](https://confluencewikidev.esri.com/display/Hub/Metric+Definition+and+Resolution) and [Stat Card & Editor documentation](https://confluencewikidev.esri.com/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=246416673).

The `arcgis-hub-resource-gallery` is used to display a simple gallery of help documents, based on tags passed into the component.

The component searches the Hub Resources group (predefined on a per environment basis) for items with the tags, and shows a very simple list of links out to the documents, pages, blogs etc.

If no items are found, or this is running in Enterprise, the component will not render anything.

### Simple Usage

This example will render the first 4 resources with the tag `userworkspace` in the Hub Resource group defined for the current environment.


```
// ... other code in component...

get resourceTags(): string[] {
  return ['userworkspace']
}

// ... other code in component...

renderResources(): VNode {
  return (<arcgis-hub-resources-gallery
    heading-text={this.intl.t('hubResources')} 
    tags={this.resourceTags} 
    limit={4}
    />)
}

```

