# hub-field-input-boundary-picker

The `hub-field-input-boundary-picker` renders a boundary picker field that allows you to select from pre-set sources or draw a custom boundary

## Usage

 The following `schema` and `uiSchema` show how you might declare this type of field when building out your editor's `schema` and `uiSchema`. They represent the `schema` and `uiSchema` for a single property: 

### `schema`

```ts
{
  type: 'object',
  properties: { // can optionally add for validation purposes
    spatialReference: { type: 'object' },
    xmax: { type: [ 'number', 'null' ] },
    xmin: { type: [ 'number', 'null' ] },
    ymax: { type: [ 'number', 'null' ] },
    ymin: { type: [ 'number', 'null' ] }
  }
}
```

### `uiSchema`

```ts
{
  ..., // see all IUiSchemaElement properties in arcgis-configuration-editor docs
  type: 'Control',  
  options: {
    ..., // see non-field specific options in arcgis-configuration-editor-field docs
    control: 'hub-field-input-boundary-picker',
    sources: [
      {
        value: 'none',
      },
      {
        selected: true,
        value: 'item',
        label: 'This is a Project',
        graphic: {
          geometry: {
            type: 'extent',
            xmin: -118,
            ymin: 30,
            xmax: -117,
            ymax: 31,
            spatialReference: {
              wkid: 4326
            }
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

#### `uiSchema.options` 
`uiSchema.options` specific to `hub-field-input-boundary-picker` 

| option | type | required | description | 
| ------ | ---- | -------- | ----------- |
| `sources` | `array` | `false` | array of sources for user to select from |

**`sources` interface:**
Based on `IBoundaryPickerSource` but with an optional `labelKey` for translation purposes:

```ts
{
  value: string,
  label?: string,
  labelKey?: string,
  graphic?: any,
  selected?: boolean
}

```

